{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789834001,"nonce":"xvkB2aaweG/4lYbntaRrQNVjd+k=","title":"`new haxe.ds.Vector\u003cT\u003e(n)` is the Int n","message":"`var v = new haxe.ds.Vector\u003cArray\u003cFloat\u003e\u003e(1); v[0]` lowers `v` to `const 1i32`: the abstract's `new` takes the one-argument value wrap in `lower_new` (the path RAYZOR_NO_XMODULE_CTOR restores) instead of calling the abstract's own constructor body (`this = new VectorData(length)`). `v[0]` then loads from address 1. Issue4986 passed at a37fcfc1 only because the loaded value fed nothing the optimizer kept; boxing the `.length` for a Dynamic parameter keeps it, and the test SIGSEGVs.\n\nAn abstract with a bodied `function new` is not a value wrap; the wrap is for `from`-only abstracts (Int64 over its class, Int32 over Int).","files":null}]}